# In a typed file a literal whose elements are all proven numbers, written to hold numbers, of which one may have a fraction, is born for doubles, as plain bears it: the read in line of a number off a list asks for that kind first..
# RUN: walk f1 mechanisms=all
# CHECK-LABEL: code f1:Body
# CHECK: = NewArray {{*}}arrayStorage=Double
# Int32s alone name nothing yet: the short literal out of registers is one call of a stub for boxed elements and for doubles; for int32 it would be an allocation, the stores and a slow way in line (a literal of three: 13 > 21 steps).
# Since the stub for short literals of int32 is back, int32s alone name their kind where the function only hands the literal on; one that it goes on using names nothing: a fraction stored into it would convert it at once.
# RUN(WHOLE): walk f2 mechanisms=all
# WHOLE-LABEL: code f2:Body
# WHOLE: = NewArray {{*}}arrayStorage=Int32
# RUN(USED): walk f6 mechanisms=all
# USED-LABEL: code f6:Body
# USED: = NewArray
# RUN(USEDSILENT): walk f6 mechanisms=all
# USEDSILENT-NOT: = NewArray {{*}}arrayStorage=
# An element that may be something else, or a list written to hold more, names nothing.
# RUN(ANYTHING): walk f3 mechanisms=all
# ANYTHING-LABEL: code f3:Body
# ANYTHING: = NewArray
# RUN(SILENT): walk f3 mechanisms=all
# SILENT-NOT: arrayStorage=
# RUN(WIDER): walk f4 mechanisms=all
# WIDER-LABEL: code f4:Body
# WIDER: = NewArray
# RUN(WIDERSILENT): walk f4 mechanisms=all
# WIDERSILENT-NOT: arrayStorage=
# In a file without types the readers of a list ask for the kind of its storage in front of their loops: a literal that is only handed on names its kind there too.
# RUN(UNTYPED): walk f5 mechanisms=all
# UNTYPED-LABEL: code f5:Body
# UNTYPED: = NewArray {{*}}arrayStorage=Double
# RUN(NONE): walk f1 mechanisms=none
# NONE-NOT: arrayStorage=

module m0 path="main.js" displayPath="main.js" body=f0
entry module=m0
function f0 module=m0 kind=Module thisType={type=anything} results=[{type=anything}] {
  b0():
    v0 = Builtin builtin=GlobalThis
    v1 = PropGet v0 key="sink" [isFreeName]
    v2 = NewClosure function=f1
    v3 = NewClosure function=f2
    v4 = NewClosure function=f3
    v5 = NewClosure function=f4
    v6 = NewClosure function=f5
    v7 = NewClosure function=f6
    v8 = Call v1, -, v2, v3, v4, v5, v6, v7
    Return v8
}
function f1 name="fractions" module=m0 flags=[IsChecked, HasExplicitName] length=1 thisType={type=anything} parameters=[{type=anything}] results=[{type=anything}] {
  b0(v0: anything):
    v1 = Integer
    v2 = BitOr v0, v1
    v3 = Double number=0.5
    v4 = Add v2, v3
    v5 = NewArray v4, v2, v3 contents=number
    Return v5
}
